# Electron security

Treat the renderer as untrusted. Privileged work belongs in the main process.

## Required direction

- Prefer `contextIsolation: true`, sandbox on, no `enableRemoteModule`
- Preload exposes thin typed wrappers only — never raw `fs`, `child_process`, or `windowManager`
- Use async `ipcMain.handle` / `ipcRenderer.invoke` instead of sync `sendSync`/`returnValue`
- Spawn processes without `shell: true`
- Validate URL schemes before `shell.openExternal`
- Validate imported settings against schema before writing userData

## Rendering user data

```javascript
// BAD — settings/profile names can become XSS into privileged preload
el.innerHTML = profile.name;
$(el).html(heading);

// GOOD
el.textContent = profile.name;
```

## Path resolution

Resolve packaged vs dev paths in one place. Do not assume `__dirname + '/../src'` is valid in both layouts.
